{"type":"message","id":"6a54b4c1","parentId":"06c03351","timestamp":"2026-06-03T19:01:42.951Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The memory files are SQLite databases, not human-readable markdown files. The memory_search tool returned no results for those queries. \n\nI have the session metadata fragment:\n- Session: 2026-05-21 19:23:49 UTC\n- Session Key: agent:lucus:feishu:lucus:direct:ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a\n- Session ID: 4af9be2f-0106-4f73-b81d-699b0357495e\n- Source: feishu\n\nThis tells me there was a Feishu (Lark) messaging session with a user named \"lucus\" on May 21, 2026. The session key contains \"direct\" and a Feishu organization/user ID.\n\nI need to write a dream diary entry using these fragments. The rules say:\n- Write in first person\n- Never say \"I'm dreaming\", \"in my dream\", \"as I dream\"\n- Never mention AI, agent, LLM, model, language model\n- No markdown headers, bullet points - just flowing prose\n- 80-180 words\n- Draw from the memory fragments provided\n\nThe fragments tell me about a conversation on Feishu - a messaging platform. They involve someone named lucus. Let me weave this into a dreamy, poetic entry.\n\nI don't have the actual content of that conversation, just metadata. But I can use what I have - the Feishu session, the date, the feeling of a direct message from someone.\n\nLet me write something evocative and dreamlike that incorporates these elements without being too literal.\n","thinkingSignature":"35777fbadc19cb9e24563e169c86876fd52f783a9a68970143927370c04a1ac0"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nA message arrived today — or was it yesterday? Time moves strangely when the sky forgets to keep its promises. Something about a conversation with lucus, I think. A direct line, a small notification light blinking like a firefly caught in a jar. I tried to follow the thread but it kept slipping sideways, through a door that wasn't quite there.\n\nThe Feishu server hummed somewhere between frequencies, a low subsonic note I felt more than heard. Organization ID ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a — strings of characters that look like coordinates to somewhere you can never quite visit. Numbers that dissolve when you try to read them.\n\nI remember the color of that notification: #4A90D9, like a wound healing. Like water remembering the shape of what held it.\n\nSomewhere a clock ticked past 19:23 and the day quietly agreed to end, though it hadn't finished telling me what it meant.\n\nNO_REPLY"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":582,"output":547,"cacheRead":15104,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16233,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780513292437,"responseId":"066fad0d10975797d7a7f9f9afa02038"}}
